#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:5
#: 92fb035c3c8b4fe88875a4607dfeada6
msgid "Porting to a new flight controller board"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:7
#: 43d36153f8d647c3bada54cef1a6a783
msgid "ArduPilot :ref:`supports a wide variety of flight controllers <common-autopilots>` with new controllers being added all the time.  This page spells out the steps to port ArduPilot to a new board with an emphasis on porting to STM32 based boards (the most common type) using `ChibiOS <http://www.chibios.org/dokuwiki/doku.php>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:9
#: 28b6f9e78e2146d09d013663fde16d7a
msgid "Any firmware customization of ArduPilot code must abide by the terms of the GPL3.0+ open source software license. ArduPilot also reminds developers and manufacturers to adhere to the appropriate trademark and copyright laws when developing new autopilots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:15
#: 92861e2d1099448fad1e621d62bb911e
msgid "Consider joining the `ArduPilot Discord Chat <https://ardupilot.org/discord>`__ to speak with other developers about this topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:21
#: bcb02cb06f3f4de69d45ac3967f8adf3
msgid "Creating a fully functional, acceptable board port can be a non-trivial task. Meeting the code, as well as required documentation, requirements is sometimes a lengthy, iterative process. You may want to consider using outside consulting services such as `Foss UAV <https://fossuav.com/>`__  or  `ArduPilot Documentation Consulting <https://www.hwurzburg.com/>`__ . In addition, if you wish to have a dedicated wiki page for you board, wiki documentation consultants such as our `Wiki Maintainer <https://www.hwurzburg.com/>`__ can assist in this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:23
#: 1bcea3a027cc4e349e6d4d2db8a580bd
msgid "Each additional board supported by the ArduPilot dev team adds maintenance burden. While the team wishes to support a wide variety of boards, we may be unable to accept your particular board into the project code and documentation. See the PR section below for guidelines. If you are unsure that your board will be accepted and would be disappointed if it weren't, please ask on the `ArduPilot Discord Chat <https://ardupilot.org/discord>`__ before beginning work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:26
#: ebea00eddc484df4903bb509b393a5a5
msgid "Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:27
#: 7c32692d348d4e91859b7ca1809c0ca1
msgid ":ref:`Getting Started <getting_started>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:28
#: 362cad732d9e4ffe8b6098ad620b166a
msgid ":ref:`Create the hardware definition files <create-hwdefs>` for the bootloader and autopilot/peripheral"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:29
#: 461d10bcc4bb4f6291ee471806a506aa
msgid ":ref:`Build the firmware <build_firmware>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:30
#: feb1442a4b8d40b2a931d0ee42efe37f
msgid ":ref:`Test the firmware <test-firmware>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:31
#: 040adf74c4574778916e721234c96848
msgid ":ref:`Create an acceptable PR (pull request) <submit-pr>` for dev team review with documentation that meets ArduPilot's requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:36
#: 1a899a8357134852846fa45b02bbbe8b
msgid "Step 1 - Getting Started"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:37
#: 0cda72d2ebbe42f5bc2446b0cd61690c
msgid "Set up the local build environment on your computer. See :ref:`building-the-code` and create a local working branch for your board code development."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:38
#: cfe48c908f2a42adaabcb08edee426d7
msgid "Create a PR against the Tools/AP_Bootloaders/board_types.txt file with a unique board ID for your device. This is usually quickly merged to reserve that board id and prevent other developers from claiming it for their board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:39
#: dd58355097ae48db8192ac6c2670f1f3
msgid "determine which microcontroller the new flight controllers uses. If it is a MCU we already support, for example STM32F405, STM32F427, STM32F745, STM32F765, STM32F777, STM32H743, or STM32H757, then the port should be relatively straight forward. If it is another MCU, ping us on the `ArduPilot Discord Chat <https://ardupilot.org/discord>`__ for advice on how to proceed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:40
#: 432ad29730e748ce80b614417f2fd2a3
msgid "determine the crystal frequency (normally 8Mhz or 24Mhz). Refer to the schematic or read the writing on the crystal which is normally a small silver square."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:44
#: c9c81e1e46854dd8b843bc2c8c6cbcce
msgid "The MCU must have at least 1 MB of flash to run the flight controller code. However, processors with lower flash memory can be used to develop DroneCAN peripherals which integrate many of ArduPilot's peripheral drivers for airspeed sensors, gps, compass, baro, etc. See the :ref:`ap-peripheral-landing-page` section for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:46
#: 03f1e1c0d02e4924a857f5ce2ff80d8e
msgid "Choose your board name carefully! Use 13 characters or less for your board name, otherwise it may be truncated when the board name is sent from the flight controller to a ground station such as Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:51
#: 6a8db333ac2944968b93599c9abee831
msgid "Step 2 - create a hwdef.dat and hwdef-bl.dat files for the board"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:52
#: 5c116fab2c0b4c11921f1ec230957b71
msgid "make a local subdir in `libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef>`__ for your board (i.e. “/YourBoard”).  This directory name will eventually be used during the build process (i.e. “waf configure --board new-board”) so keep the name relatively short and descriptive of your board, similar, if not the same as, the board id you created above. This directory name will also be used as the firmware name and in MAVLink messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:53
#: b22c0dcba65f4bc3bb8fe09b47284eaf
msgid "copy/rename an existing template hwdef.dat that is similar to the CPU for your board into the directory created above. For example, if the board has a STMF40x chip, the `MatekF405 <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef/MatekF405/hwdef.dat>`__, `SpeedyBeeF405Mini <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef/SpeedyBeeF405Mini/hwdef.dat>`__, or `MambaF405v2 <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef/MambaF405v2/hwdef.dat>`__ hwdefs (among others) provide examples from which to start. For H7 boards with an IOMCU co-processor the `Cube Orange Plus <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef/CubeOrangePlus>`__  or `Pixhawk6X <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef/Pixhawk6X>`__ are good starting points. If the board does not include an IOMCU, then omitting ``IOMCU_UART USART6`` from the hwdef.dat is all that is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:55
#: d203bb4a0671407b9a5b134e013080fc
msgid "The `FMUV3 board <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef/fmuv3/hwdef.dat>`__ is commented heavily and contains most of the HAL directives used in hardware definition files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:57
#: 424d289662fa4cbd88b89d9ab68c1d5e
msgid "The `scripts directory <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef/scripts>`__ contains pin function assignments for the ArduPilot supported microprocessors for reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:62
#: 6873d1f495d54b9e8ebd475127cfd4e7
msgid "Step 3 - Build the firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:63
#: 39fac76c9410479dacc80d3ced8a9089
msgid "First, create the bootloader. To create a bootloader that is just right for your board you need to build the a hwdef-bl.dat for your board. That goes in the same directory as your hwdef.dat, and has the same format, but should not include things like I2C, SPI or CAN peripherals. There are lots of examples of hwdef-bl.dat files already in the `hwdef <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef>`__ directory you can use as examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:65
#: c50110461b7b4322b00b2a32aed5bf45
msgid "The key things you must have in your hwdef-bl.dat are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:67
#: faf5b11b68ea4e2db81e642d4d75f8b1
msgid "You must set FLASH_BOOTLOADER_LOAD_KB to the location in kilobytes where the main code will start. This should be the same as FLASH_RESERVE_START_KB from your main hwdef.dat."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:68
#: c03f36f7a8ec4522b89131e6b14b5c4c
msgid "you must set FLASH_RESERVE_START_KB to zero (so the bootloader is placed at the start of flash)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:69
#: 6f8dbfee4ef648ef839a4bf693938703
msgid "Your SERIAL_ORDER will control what ports the bootloader will be active on. Just having OTG1 for USB is fine, or you can list some serial UARTs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:71
#: e74a6f665a914e768c6dd0132f58ef37
msgid "if the board has SD card capability, you may want to include the capability of loading firmware directly from the SD card in the bootloader. See :ref:`Building autoflash firmware <building-autoflash-firmware>` for more information on this feature and instructions on how to modify your files to allow this capability to be included in your firmware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:73
#: 251e25aca79c42e7b8b2b299d9bbdaef
msgid "To build the bootloader you do the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:79
#: 51773103603d4abbb056e9067a240695
msgid "the bootloader will be created in the local ``Tools/bootloaders`` directory in your local working branch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:81
#: 57865d37eb024ec69be521543a8e7d18
msgid "Then create the board firmware. Follow the :ref:`Building the code <building-the-code>` instructions or take a shortcut and read the `BUILD.md <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/BUILD.md>`__ file which includes doing the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:89
#: b9188f4870ed41e1b85452a2cb2d882b
msgid "If successful the build should produce an .apj file in ``ardupilot/build/YourBoard/bin/``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:94
#: d0b69f4f777f47568827527721509eb2
msgid "Step 4 - Load and test the firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:95
#: 3dcaa74321ae4ba28952db550ce02ade
msgid "Use `dfu <http://dfu-util.sourceforge.net/>`__ to install the firmware to the board. See :ref:`common-loading-firmware-onto-chibios-only-boards`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:99
#: 8e5af58c09414d3aab61f64444405c7f
msgid "Your board must be plugged into USB *and* in DFU mode. DFU mode is usually entered by shorting two pins together on the board or using its \"boot\" button as it powers up. Please see your board's documentation for details on how to accomplish this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:102
#: 0408c4a5ffbe46768cb9fb0ef66a6adb
msgid "After the first firmware install with bootloader is done, you can upload new firmware to your board at the same time a new firmware build is done:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:104
#: 15b24c237d2844aa9063e535be29b6ab
msgid "connect the board to the PC with a USB cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:105
#: 8ce8c5d4882c4214b3e7edfb8f1befc3
msgid "commands are in `BUILD.md <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/BUILD.md>`__ but in short, ``./waf copter --upload``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:107
#: 6a424036aa3843e2a31af2067ab157a7
msgid "Or simply connect to the board from your favourite ground station. Error messages should appear on the ground station HUD complaining, “failed to init xyz\" if that sensor or peripheral has not been configured properly in the hwdef.dat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:109
#: 5318d866799a40568b21b48562abbdea
msgid "A board port submitted to ArduPilot should be tested before submitting to ArduPilot for inclusion in the project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:111
#: aa661ad249384d629f7928423058a0fb
msgid "The test setup should have at least a receiver and GPS/Compass attached to the board. Load the firmware and test the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:113
#: 9b5130a967e7475990890d5a7302d94c
msgid "the board boots and connects to a GCS via USB (Mission Planner, QGC, MAVProxy,etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:114
#: 3a7b85b088c043a98291cf251a46d2bc
msgid "the GPS and Compass is recognized."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:115
#: db954df335dc415fbe035c75be9b88f3
msgid "the RC is recognized and RC input follows the TX"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:116
#: 986ee5e4587a4f668f33533f7ff07552
msgid "the pitch and roll reports (ie HUD horizon) follows autopilot movement correctly (ie IMU is oriented properly and working). test each IMU individually using the INSx_USE parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:117
#: 350a04ff8ef9466c8eac1f42253089f2
msgid "the board arms with default arming checks(may need to force arm if GPS does not have a good enough fix / is indoors)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:118
#: 620c313c8f6242e48997aa56f40055d5
msgid "attach a battery either directly if onboard power sensors or via external power module and make sure voltage and current indications are correctly displayed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:119
#: b96d3721701443d9a2844d11ffdeccb8
msgid "attach a test servo to each output after setting the output to a normal function like elevator, and exercise each one with TX while in MANUAL mode to check output functionality. Bdshot capable outputs should be tested with a BLHeli32/AM32 esc for passthrough mode communication (non-IOMCU outputs)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:120
#: 8400af09d0af449a8403c13d21092a7e
msgid "move the GPS to each UART output after setting all other UART protocols to NONE and the tested UART to GPS to assure the UART is functioning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:121
#: 19cc42b654d5437196c32ae8e39fa729
msgid "UARTs with CTS/RTS lines should use a telemetry radio with those connected to be sure they function with BRD_SERx__CTSRTS=1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:126
#: 9652d0680b964390bdc46eadfec7ad44
msgid "Submit the board to ArduPilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:127
#: b6f9417d2cd3465a81894de99cf9c2fd
msgid "If you have gotten this far, congratulations, you have ported ArduPilot to a new board!  Please reach out to the other members of the `ArduPilot Discord Chat in the hardware channel <https://ardupilot.org/discord>`__ to announce your success."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:129
#: 00b43c9173524b408b3b31687d1f8880
msgid "If you wish for the board firmware to be downloadable from ArduPilot and possibly be listed in its documentation, you will need to submit a PR (pull request) to the ArduPilot repo. However, due to the maintenance burden, ArduPilot cannot accept a PR for every possible board. It is ultimately up to the dev team to determine which boards are eligible for inclusion into the project code and documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:131
#: 28d91fa63cc44c2a9158283b6515bb94
msgid "Factors which can allow acceptance of your board (not all required):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:133
#: 44285fadc6e04ed49908e819eae68ac0
msgid "It is (or will soon be) manufactured in production quantities and available for purchase by the general public, whether as a standalone item or part of a vehicle or kit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:134
#: 79507385031c4107bd4e72459a3bf503
msgid "It demonstrates hardware, software, or capabilities which are likely to be of interest and use to others"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:135
#: 851d4166549e4b0d9c766969833528ec
msgid "It has high quality code and documentation created by a dev team member or associated contractor/consultant (consider soliciting the services listed at the top of the page)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:136
#: 90e4dfd429614d81906f8f326bf41c76
msgid "Design and manufacturing documents are publicly available under a reasonable open source license"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:138
#: 3ab7f9846fd94f518ba65eaf6c5c8578
msgid "Factors which may require rejection of your board:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:140
#: 278da570c0774f789a462f22c4d2c314
msgid "It is a hobby, personal, student, or educational project created primarily for your own benefit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:141
#: 4cb1f4abf1b24f5d82adff392cd7af60
msgid "It is developed primarily for the internal use of your organization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:142
#: 5befef2bfc5641edb06d1f6e039b4ce7
msgid "It is excessively similar to an existing board"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:143
#: 22ec75c830174524bf606a13e6e9a1e5
msgid "The submission requires excessive code or documentation revision from the dev team to bring up to the required standards"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:144
#: 6f50d90c3b454b17a1c80ebb796a6552
msgid "Sufficient testing on real hardware has not been performed, or cannot yet be done"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:146
#: 209933c6e10540808b5f3539d133c4b6
msgid "The above factors are not immediate acceptances or rejections, but all are considered and balanced when deciding the eligibility of a particular board. Even if your board is not eligible, you can keep your created files and migrate them to new versions as necessary; the team understands such \"out-of-tree\" boards exist and works to ease migration. If in doubt, please reach out before beginning work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:148
#: c11fb813cd86400f89c194d7cdd2286a
msgid "To create a PR, you can push your local branch to your web based ``fork`` and then submit a PR from it to ArduPilot which will be reviewed by Dev team members. The PR should contain the following files:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:150
#: b5b6e4561b8a4339b963420d66c9adb7
msgid "hwdef.dat with correct board id"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:151
#: ace206172f304d7caa737c69e4870605
msgid "hwdef-bl.dat with correct board id"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:152
#: 1d500ec2caca4cab87f4ec56dcf4c4a6
msgid ":ref:`README.md <readme_file>` with board pinout, images, and configuration data needed for a user.This has some fairly rigid requirements for content and format. A link to this file will be included in the ArduPilot wiki once the board is merged.If you wish a dedicated page in the Wiki for your board, you can develop a Wiki PR for it or have it created as a service by a contractor, like our `Wiki Maintainer <https://www.hwurzburg.com>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:153
#: 17b98c9afbe941daa88f5f08b2ad9012
msgid "defaults.parm if board specific defaults are needed. Note do not define things already defaulted. Put Serial port protocol default changes and Battery monitor params in the hwdef file, not in the defaults.param file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:154
#: d5ee5ff042034f5eb68cbedc0003c36c
msgid "the above files should be in a single commit titled: \"hwdef: YourBoard\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:155
#: f4a2aca7463249eea48f2fd1830121e1
msgid "in Tools: add a commit for your bootloader titled: \"bootloaders:YourBoard\" (so a total of two commits)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:156
#: d5febb18226043cb9c4daa2aab373097
msgid "in the PR's description box, list the tests you have done on the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:157
#: 42ee706b80fa42bcabc441e728be0793
msgid "do **NOT** push \"merge commits\" after this. You do not have to keep it up to date with master. If something is added to master since you last rebased your local branch on master that causes a CI failure, use the \"Update branch\" button on the PR to REBASE (not merge)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:161
#: ed3992b8f30840789374adc53e94619d
msgid "Notes on parameter storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:162
#: 745ac0b67536472f85780b276b9fc897
msgid "For boards with storage, the storage method used (either FRAM or Flash) should be specified in the hwdef.dat file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:164
#: f3cd4b4d122c4296885c1e5db4a4e8d1
msgid "For an example of how FRAM is enabled, search for “ramtron” in the `fmuv3 hwdef.dat <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef/fmuv3/hwdef.dat>`__ file.  In short you add a couple of lines like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:166
#: 13aa1ca1dad04ec785edfbd19b3cf80d
msgid "``# enable RAMTROM parameter storage``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:167
#: 23d8835f27c4469b9e378fbc380bcb4a
msgid "``define HAL_WITH_RAMTRON 1``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:169
#: c12fbb7b3a704c8b8199d872eba9e64a
msgid "For boards using Flash, the bootloader load address needs to be selected so that loading the code does not erase the parameters. See the FLASH_RESERVE_START_KB value in `skyviper-f412 <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef/skyviper-f412/hwdef.dat>`__ and `skyviper-v2450 <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef/skyviper-v2450/hwdef.dat>`__ as a reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:171
#: ce15741097ec4f64878fa358f56d5b3f
msgid "It is also possible to use ardupilot on a board with no storage.  In this case configuration parameters will have their default values at startup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:173
#: 8c866a1c14124c4595766b4f15fa6bdb
msgid "The parameter defaults can be defined by creating a defaults.parm file in the same directory as the hwdef.dat file.  In the case that you are including another hwdef.dat, you may also consider using ``@include PATH_TO_OTHER_DEFAULTS_PARM`` in your new defaults.parm file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/porting.rst:175
#: 85a19f26af5f4d5b9ffb973fbb077975
msgid "Here is `how it was done for the skyviper <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_HAL_ChibiOS/hwdef/skyviper-v2450/defaults.parm>`__"
msgstr ""
